WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.512
Exemptions expire.

2
00:00:01.512 --> 00:00:06.162
Learn's page on the Azure Policy
exemption structure gives two categories:

3
00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:09.462
Mitigated, when the policy's
intent is met another way,

4
00:00:09.462 --> 00:00:12.762
and Waiver, when non-compliance
is accepted for a time.

5
00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:17.124
Every exemption gets an expiry and
a reference to its decision record.

6
00:00:17.124 --> 00:00:21.845
And once it expires, Learn says it's kept
for the record but no longer honored,

7
00:00:21.845 --> 00:00:24.662
so the resource shows
as non-compliant again.

8
00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:29.775
The guide adds a rule: exemptions
only, never not-scopes for convenience.

9
00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:32.795
Each month, export
compliance: the summary,

10
00:00:32.795 --> 00:00:36.937
and the list of non-compliant
resources, filed as evidence.

11
00:00:36.937 --> 00:00:39.736
Rollback, if enforcement breaks something,

12
00:00:39.736 --> 00:00:43.000
is the assignment back to
do-not-enforce, in minutes.

13
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.460
One caution: resources a remediation task
created stay until someone removes them.
